    fix(admissions): name the true producer, restore dropped contract pins
    
    authoring_command was a hardcoded "python3 scripts/run_all.py" -- a
    command that never calls gen_admission.py, so it could not have
    produced the receipt bytes it appears in. Emit and check the real
    producer, skills/<skill>/scripts/gen_admission.py, per skill.
    
    build_receipt() derives contract_files solely from skill.json's own
    shared_contracts. Four skill.json files never declared
    admission.schema.json and source-lock.schema.json there -- pins the
    old, hand-authored receipts carried out-of-band -- so the automated
    stamper silently dropped them, and check_admissions.py's
    listed-entries-only comparison can't see a removal. Add the two schema
    paths to feature-map-engineering, control-backup, control-code-intel,
    and spatial-loop-grounded's shared_contracts, matching control-noodle's
    already-complete list.
    
    skill.json is itself inside a Skill's subject_files, so widening
    shared_contracts moved feature-map-engineering's skill_tree_sha256;
    re-pin it in control-noodle's domain/composition.json and its
    fixtures/valid/procedure-admission.json fixture (fail-closed, not a
    new problem: control-noodle's validator refuses on the stale pin
    either way).
    
    Also scope admission_stamp.py's docstring: the refusal is structural
    for the stamp() path only, not a guarantee about how the file at
    admissions/<skill>.json got there -- filed ed3c/skill-concerns#42 for
    closing that gap at the CI trust boundary.
    
    Regenerated all five admissions/*.json through the guarded stamper.

